The states of a record, in one of its fields, and the ways between them.

```
use ravenrs_app::{EntityInfo, EnumOption, FieldInfo, FieldKind, StateMachine};

let options = vec![EnumOption::new("draft", "Draft"), EnumOption::new("done", "Done")];
let entity = EntityInfo::new("Task")
    .field(FieldInfo::new("id", FieldKind::Integer).key())
    .field(FieldInfo::new("state", FieldKind::Enum(options)))
    .state_machine(
        StateMachine::new("state").state("draft", "Draft").state("done", "Done").start("draft").transition(
            "draft",
            "done",
            "Finish",
        ),
    );
assert!(entity.check().is_ok());
```

6825.docs:
The model of a business application, with no GUI: entities, a layered application
model, object spaces, actions, controllers, frames and modules.

```
use ravenrs_app::{EntityInfo, FieldInfo, FieldKind, MemoryDatabase, ModelLayers, ModelLayer, ObjectSpace, generate_model};

let account = EntityInfo::new("Account")
    .caption("Conta")
    .navigation("Cadastros")
    .field(FieldInfo::new("id", FieldKind::Integer).key())
    .field(FieldInfo::new("name", FieldKind::Text).caption("Nome").default_property());

// The model: a list, a form and a place in the navigation, changed by a layer.
let mut layers = ModelLayers::new(generate_model(std::slice::from_ref(&account))?);
layers.set(&ModelLayer::User, &["NavigationItems", "Cadastros"], "Caption", "Registros".into());
let model = layers.merged();
assert_eq!(model.root.at(&["NavigationItems", "Cadastros"]).and_then(|n| n.text("Caption")), Some("Registros"));

// The records: nothing is kept until the commit.
let mut space = MemoryDatabase::new(vec![account])?.space();
let mut object = space.new_object("Account")?;
object.set("name", "Corrente");
space.save(object)?;
assert!(space.is_modified());
space.commit()?;
# Ok::<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>>(())
```

1031.docs:
A button whose work runs away from the screen, on a thread of its own: it shows how far it
got, can be stopped, and what it hands back is kept on the screen's thread. While it runs,
the action is off, so it never runs twice at once.

```
use ravenrs_app::{Action, Selection};

let archive = Action::background("Archive", "Arquivar", |job| {
    for record in job.selected() {
        let mut record = record.clone();
        record.set("Archived", true);
        job.save(record);
    }
    Ok(())
})
.selection(Selection::RequireMultiple);
assert!(archive.is_background());
```

5304.docs:
The entities of a Rust source file: each struct with `#[derive(BusinessObject)]`, its enum
fields taken from the enums with `#[derive(BusinessEnum)]` in the same file. What the
derive refuses is refused here, with the same words; what only a compiler could work out,
such as a default that calls a function, is refused too, with its place.

```
let entities = ravenrs_app::entities_from_source(
    r#"
    #[derive(BusinessEnum)]
    enum Kind { Checking, Savings }

    #[derive(BusinessObject)]
    #[object(caption = "Accounts")]
    struct Account {
        #[field(key)]
        id: i64,
        #[field(caption = "Kind")]
        kind: Kind,
    }
    "#,
)
.map_err(|errors| errors[0].to_string())?;
assert_eq!(entities[0].name, "Account");
# Ok::<(), String>(())
```

1059.docs:
Runs as an update: sets fields of every record selected of this entity, as
`field = expression; ...`, each read from the record as it was; checks them against the
rules of `Save`, and keeps them all or none. What does not parse, or names a field the
entity has not, is found when the application is put together.

```
use ravenrs_app::{Action, EntityInfo, FieldInfo, FieldKind, Selection};

let task = EntityInfo::new("Task")
    .field(FieldInfo::new("id", FieldKind::Integer).key())
    .field(FieldInfo::new("state", FieldKind::Text));
let finish = Action::simple("Finish", "Concluir")
    .target_entity("Task")
    .selection(Selection::RequireMultiple)
    .assign(&task, "state = 'done'");
assert_eq!(finish.caption(), "Concluir");
```

